.env
# No trailing slash: the worktree convention symlinks backend/venv rather than
# creating a real directory, and "venv/" (dir-only) does not match a symlink --
# confirmed live across 27 worktrees carrying an untracked "backend/venv" this
# way. "venv" (no slash) matches both a real dir and a symlink.
venv
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
*.db
# SQLite WAL sidecars. app/db.py puts every local sqlite database into WAL mode
# (see _apply_sqlite_concurrency_pragmas), which makes SQLite keep aladdin2.db-wal
# and aladdin2.db-shm alongside the database for as long as anything is connected
# — and after a crash. "*.db" above does NOT cover those names, so without these
# two lines they show up as untracked files and can be committed by accident.
# They are transient engine state, never results.
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# Raw SEC EDGAR companyfacts JSON cache (refetchable vendor input, not results)
data/edgar_companyfacts/
# Parsed SEC Insider Transactions Data Sets cache, 6.3MB (refetchable vendor
# input, not results -- fetch_insider_trades rebuilds it from sec.gov in ~82
# rate-limited requests; the RESULTS live in cross_sectional_trial_results)
data/insider_form4_trades.csv.gz
data/insider_form4_trades.csv.report.json
# SEC EDGAR filing narrative-text cache, ~0.6GB gzipped at full-universe scale
# (refetchable vendor input, not results -- EdgarFilingTextProvider rebuilds it
# from www.sec.gov/Archives; an archived filing is immutable so the cache needs
# no age bound. The RESULTS live in cross_sectional_trial_results and
# data/research_runs/lazy_prices_*.txt)
data/edgar_filing_text/
# Binance USDT-perp funding/kline CSV cache, ~19MB (refetchable vendor input,
# not results -- BinanceFuturesProvider rebuilds it from the keyless public
# fapi endpoints; the RESULTS live in cross_sectional_trial_results and
# data/research_runs/funding_carry_*.txt)
data/binance_futures/
# Raw SEC Form 13F structured-data-set ZIPs + fails-to-deliver ZIPs, ~2.7GB
# (refetchable vendor input, not results -- Form13FProvider rebuilds it from
# sec.gov's own published index; the RESULTS live in cross_sectional_trial_results
# and data/research_runs/best_ideas_13f_*.txt)
data/form13f_raw/
# SEC EDGAR Item 2.02 announcement-calendar cache for the earnings-
# announcement-premium family, ~4MB (refetchable vendor input, not results --
# data/research_runs/fetch_eap_announcement_calendar.py rebuilds it from
# sec.gov; the RESULTS live in cross_sectional_trial_results and
# data/research_runs/earnings_announcement_premium_*.txt)
data/eap_edgar_announcement_calendar.json
# Raw FINRA bi-monthly equity short interest files, ~366MB across 208 settlement
# cycles (refetchable vendor input, not results -- FinraShortInterestProvider
# rebuilds it from cdn.finra.org; an archived cycle file is immutable so the
# cache needs no age bound. The RESULTS live in cross_sectional_trial_results
# and data/research_runs/short_interest_*.txt)
data/finra_short_interest/
# SEC XBRL frames cache for dei:EntityCommonStockSharesOutstanding, ~37 quarterly
# JSON files (refetchable vendor input, not results -- SecSharesOutstandingProvider
# rebuilds it from data.sec.gov in ~37 requests)
data/sec_shares_outstanding/
# yfinance ex-dividend-date calendar cache for the dividend-month-premium
# family, ~0.5MB (refetchable vendor input, not results --
# data/research_runs/fetch_dividend_calendar.py rebuilds it from Yahoo's
# corporate-actions feed in ~30s; the RESULTS live in
# cross_sectional_trial_results and
# data/research_runs/dividend_month_premium_*.txt)
data/dividend_month_ex_date_calendar.json
# Dividend PAYMENT-date calendar for the dividend-payment-pressure family,
# ~2.8MB (refetchable vendor input, not results --
# data/research_runs/fetch_dividend_payment_calendar.py rebuilds it in ~25min
# from four sources: Yahoo's corporate-actions feed for ex-dates and amounts,
# Yahoo's per-ticker .calendar for the ex->pay lag, Nasdaq's dividend-history
# API for ground-truth pay/declaration dates, and SEC company-concept frames
# for share counts. Most of that wall clock is the Nasdaq pass, which is one
# request per ticker and refuses NYSE names. The RESULTS live in
# cross_sectional_trial_results and
# data/research_runs/dividend_payment_pressure_*.txt)
data/dividend_payment_calendar.json
# Point-in-time raw price store, ~120MB at full 768-name/11-year scale
# (price_store.py). UNLIKE every other entry in this file this one is NOT
# simply "refetchable vendor input": a rebuild re-asks Yahoo, and Yahoo's
# answer for an ALREADY-STORED date can have changed since — which is the
# whole reason the store exists. What survives a wipe is close but not
# identical, so a wipe forfeits bit-exact reproduction of any result computed
# before it. It is still gitignored because ~120MB of vendor rows does not
# belong in git history; the durable RESULTS live in
# cross_sectional_trial_results and data/research_runs, and a rebuild is
# recorded by price_store.write_store_manifest so a run can say which store
# state produced it.
data/price_store/
# Filtered SEC Form N-PORT bulk extractions, ~250MB across 27 quarterly data
# sets (refetchable vendor input, not results -- NportProvider rebuilds it from
# sec.gov's own DERA bulk ZIPs via HTTP range requests, ~7GB of transfer for
# ~250MB of kept rows, and an archived quarterly data set is immutable so the
# cache needs no age bound. The RESULTS live in cross_sectional_trial_results
# and data/research_runs/nport_flow_fit_*.txt)
data/nport_bulk/
# The union (S&P 500 + S&P 600) cache the Coval-Stafford fire-sale family
# fetches; same rationale as data/nport_bulk/ above, separate directory
# because the CUSIP filter differs (see fetch_nport_bulk_firesale.py).
data/nport_bulk_firesale/
# 15-minute Alpaca SIP bars for PHASE_B_UNIVERSE_15MIN (284 tickers,
# 2021-01-04..2026-08-24), ~1GB (refetchable vendor input, not results --
# data/research_runs/fetch_intraday_bars_15min.py rebuilds it from
# data.alpaca.markets in ~1-2h via AlpacaProvider.get_stock_bars).
#
# THIS ENTRY EXISTS BECAUSE THE ABSENCE OF ONE ALREADY COST A REAL RESULT.
# The 2026-08-26 low_frequency_patterns screening run cached these same bars
# in a SESSION SCRATCHPAD (/private/tmp/claude-501/<session-uuid>/scratchpad/
# bars_cache, see research_archive/session_2026-08-22_to_27/fetch_bars.py:33).
# That directory is ephemeral and is now gone, so the original run's exact
# inputs are unrecoverable and its numbers cannot be bit-reproduced -- only
# re-measured against a fresh fetch. A durable, explicitly-ignored path under
# data/ is the fix: refetchable input stays out of git history, but it stops
# evaporating between sessions. The RESULTS live in
# cross_sectional_trial_results and
# data/research_runs/low_frequency_patterns_*.txt.
data/intraday_bars_15min/
# Daily per-contract futures settlement/price caches for the TSMOM universe
# (refetchable vendor input, not results): cme_span/ is rebuilt from CME's
# public SPAN archive by data/research_runs/fetch_cme_span_archive.py
# (~3,200 FTP GETs, ~40 GB of transfer for ~130 MB of kept rows); eia/ from
# eia.gov by eia_nymex_futures.fetch_all; databento/ from Databento with a
# key. The RESULTS live in data/research_runs/futures_data_sourcing_*.txt.
data/futures_daily/

# Per-fund, per-asset-category N-PORT portfolio totals, used by the
# Frazzini-Lamont "Dumb Money" family to identify DOMESTIC EQUITY funds (the
# paper's own universe restriction, JFE 88(2) p.302). Derived data, ~17min to
# rebuild from SEC's public bulk ZIPs by
# data/research_runs/fetch_nport_fund_asset_categories.py; same rationale as
# data/nport_bulk/ above. The RESULTS live in
# data/research_runs/frazzini_lamont_dumb_money_*.
data/nport_fund_asset_categories/
# The source PDFs of the paper itself; re-downloadable from the URLs pinned
# (with sha256s) in frazzini_lamont_dumb_money_SOURCES.md. The extracted text
# that was actually read IS committed alongside it.
data/research_runs/dumbmoney_src/*.pdf
